#!/usr/bin/env harding
#
# Overflow.hrd - Overflow class.

Overflow := ArithmeticError derive
# Overflow reports integer arithmetic that leaves the 64-bit range.
# Harding integers are fixed width, so a result that would exceed them cannot be
# represented; the operation signals this class instead of wrapping silently.
# It sits under ArithmeticError beside DivisionByZero.
# Before this class existed the condition surfaced as an uncatchable VM error
# string, so on: Error do: could not intercept it.
